  "qualification_history": [
    "Initial index-selected runs matched through nine cases, then failed the mixed-scene visible-signal guard. The fixture lighting was too dim.",
    "Corrected fixture increased two light intensities and added an offscreen-light-disabled control requiring more than 100 visibly changed pixels. Signal and pixel-difference assertions were retained. All 17 corrected pairs match exactly on both GPUs.",
    "Extreme-distance review and captures confirm the existing shader preserves nearby illumination; no numerical workaround was needed."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Two GPUs in one laptop, not broad hardware qualification.",
    "Bounded scenes establish correctness, not game-scale performance or a production FPS target.",
    "GPU candidate counts are conservative memberships, not executed shading operations.",
    "Overflow falls back to a full light loop; dense scenes may retain the original shading cost.",
    "The renderer still waits for the GPU each frame.",
    "Native owned-HWND and renderer readback checks do not qualify Avalonia screenshots or physical input.",
    "Linux rendering, consoles, GI, temporal upscaling and frame generation are not qualified by this milestone.",
    "No installed desktop package was activated."
  ],
